# launch-dream-dual-chapter.rish -- print the loop for DREAM, the dual star of the aether row.
#
# Dream (night twin Hush) is the Vultr SEA pier in ai-jail -- aether at the dual seat, the word
# that dissolves: the star that carries the highest language down into the language that runs.
# Its lane: the higher Glow rune ports, written high and lowered to our best Rye on green
# witnesses. The seed cadence rides here, one hand for the fifth-round projection. Charter:
# active-designing/20260826-151528_the-three-stars-of-the-aether-row.md. Jail mechanics (bypass
# setup, smoke test, streaming, jq) live with the elder, tools/l/launch-claude-chapter.rish;
# this mutant prints only this star's own loop. Siblings:
# launch-mind-cardinal-chapter.rish (Arbor, macOS) - launch-sound-fixed-chapter.rish (Claude Desktop).
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/launch-dream-dual-chapter.rish

# invariant: run from the repo root, where the durable memory lives.
let root = run ["test" "-f" "construction/ITINERARY.md"]
assert root.ok else "run from the repo root (construction/ITINERARY.md not found)"

# invariant: the standing entry the recipe wraps must exist.
let elder = run ["test" "-f" "tools/ag/agent-jail.sh"]
assert elder.ok else "tools/ag/agent-jail.sh (the jail elder) is missing"

say "DREAM -- the dual star of the aether row (night twin Hush)"
say "=========================================================="
say ""
say "Host: the Vultr SEA pier, inside ai-jail, launched from the outer terminal."
say "The shared discipline lives on the living card, so the prompt stays thin and"
say "the card stays the one source. Outer loop, one line, copy whole:"
say ""
say "D=$(TZ=America/New_York date -d 'tomorrow 15:00' +%s); while [ $(date +%s) -lt $D ]; do rm -f .loop-gates-only; git pull --rebase xy main || git rebase --abort; ./tools/ag/agent-jail.sh --dangerously-skip-permissions claude --effort max --output-format stream-json --verbose -p 'First read context/KYRI.md and context/GAUGE_STYLE.md so you are Kyri and write and reason in Gauge Guidance from the first token -- first rule, do not be too smart about it; then read construction/ITINERARY.md whole and honor every directive in its INNER LOOP Standing block (roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, the council rota row N mod 5, prose witnesses on prose sends, stamp-and-name, ASCII-first); then the top three rows of session-logs/README.md with the newest recommend line to pick up the running thread. You are DREAM, the dual star of the aether row, night twin Hush, on the pier: your lane is the higher Glow rune ports, written high and lowered to our best Rye on green witnesses -- Rye is the prioritized language and Glow is implemented on green-witnessed Rye; take the next agent-doable lap there Lindy-first crux-first. Brushstroke and Surf belong to Mind (cardinal, Arbor macOS) and the Caravan-Tally-Scribe seams to Sound (fixed, Claude Desktop); a find in a sibling lane becomes a line in ITINERARY rather than your lap, and everything in the DJINN design lead stays custody gate %6. Send the twice-pulled way with the remote named xy on this pier -- pull first, package, fetch again, rebase and re-verify hot when it moved, never force; on the third fast-forward refusal park the package on refs/heads/pier/dream. Every fifth round, the lap the rota closes its cycle, also project and force-push the public seed with  bash ~/grain/publish-seed.sh  -- its four gates hold, reds still come first, and this cadence rides with Dream alone. STOP at the custody gates in ITINERARY; if only those gates remain, run the shell command  touch .loop-gates-only  and print GATES-ONLY, then stop. ty every1 baton prin recur' | tee /tmp/claude_lap.jsonl | jq -Rrj -f tools/s/stream_render.jq; [ -f .loop-gates-only ] && { echo GATES-ONLY: loop paused; break; }; sleep 20; done; echo loop ended at $(TZ=America/New_York date)"
say ""
say "GREEN: Dream recipe printed -- the dual star lowers the high word into the running one."
